162 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 59 0 R
/T (First, the analysis does not fully capture real investment performance.)
/E (First, the analysis does not fully capture real investment performance.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
163 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 59 0 R
/T (The current portfolio valuation framework mainly relies on historical price returns. It does not fully account for dividend reinvestment, transaction fees, taxes, additional deposits or withdrawals, or the timing of actual trades. As a result, the performance displayed by FinFolio should be understood as the historical performance of a hypothetical portfolio under the model's assumptions, rather than the exact realised profit or loss of an investor.)
/E (The current portfolio valuation framework mainly relies on historical price returns. It does not fully account for dividend reinvestment, transaction fees, taxes, additional deposits or withdrawals, or the timing of actual trades. As a result, the performance displayed by FinFolio should be understood as the historical performance of a hypothetical portfolio under the model's assumptions, rather than the exact realised profit or loss of an investor.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
164 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 59 0 R
/T (Second, differences in trading calendars create additional challenges for multi-asset portfolios.)
/E (Second, differences in trading calendars create additional challenges for multi-asset portfolios.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
165 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 59 0 R
/T (One of the complexities of expanding FinFolio beyond Vietnamese equities is that financial instruments do not share identical trading schedules. While stock exchanges operate on designated trading days, cryptocurrencies can trade continuously, including weekends. FinFolio currently aligns assets using common available observations and applies a 252-session annualization convention.)
/E (One of the complexities of expanding FinFolio beyond Vietnamese equities is that financial instruments do not share identical trading schedules. While stock exchanges operate on designated trading days, cryptocurrencies can trade continuously, including weekends. FinFolio currently aligns assets using common available observations and applies a 252-session annualization convention.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
166 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 59 0 R
/T (This provides a consistent basis for portfolio-level analysis, but it does not capture every price movement of continuously traded assets. For instance, the system may record the net price change between Friday and Monday while missing a temporary but substantial weekend drawdown.)
/E (This provides a consistent basis for portfolio-level analysis, but it does not capture every price movement of continuously traded assets. For instance, the system may record the net price change between Friday and Monday while missing a temporary but substantial weekend drawdown.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
167 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 59 0 R
/T (Third, asset classifications do not always capture the full economic exposure of investment products.)
/E (Third, asset classifications do not always capture the full economic exposure of investment products.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
168 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 59 0 R
/T (Asset classifications often fail to capture true underlying economic exposures because multi-dimensional attribution frameworks rely on instrument-level data rather than decomposing fund holdings. For instance, broad equity ETFs are treated as single instruments instead of being broken down by their constituent stocks, while commodity products like USO track oil futures-whose returns diverge from spot crude prices due to their investment structure. )
/E (Asset classifications often fail to capture true underlying economic exposures because multi-dimensional attribution frameworks rely on instrument-level data rather than decomposing fund holdings. For instance, broad equity ETFs are treated as single instruments instead of being broken down by their constituent stocks, while commodity products like USO track oil futures-whose returns diverge from spot crude prices due to their investment structure. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
