/Count -2
/Next 439 0 R
>>
endobj
500 0 obj
<<
/Title (Asset classifications often fail to capture true underlying economic exposures because multi-dimensional attribution frameworks rely on instrument-level data rather than decomposing fund holdings. For instance, broad equity ETFs are treated as single instruments instead of being broken down by their constituent stocks, while commodity products like USO track oil futures-whose returns diverge from spot crude prices due to their investment structure.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 439 0 R
>>
endobj
